  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kanyele Maize Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Maize.Beneficiaries: 167 smallholder farmers.Kanyele AMCOS is a resilient and remote farmer organization whose purpose is to develop a strong and growing maize value chain to increase members incomes and build stronger and sustainable rural community in Rukwa Region, Kalambo District 1,500km from Dar es Salaam. The organization has within 4 years grown its membership from 30 to 212 currently and growing. They have managed to bulk together 480MT and successfully supplied to the National Food Reserve Agency between 2015 and 2016. The organization has experienced fluctuating maize prices, a situation that has impacted negatively on farmers incomes. Now the organization has entered into a contract with Mbasira Food Industries Ltd, a Sumbawanga based bulk buyer and processor of maize to supply 600MT during the current season to commence in June 2018. The order guarantees the organization a premium price of Tzs 10/kg above the prevailing market price at the time of supply. This supply arrangement calls for enhancing the AMCOS organizational, financial and agricultural capacities through USADF OAG. Members will need more training in good agricultural practices, post harvest handling of maize through appropriate storage to mimize losses as well as having in place an inputs revolving fund to ensure timely availability of inputs. A technical team to facilitate and capacitate the organization to fulfill its supply obligations would be recommended recourse.</narrative>
  </description>
